+# UI Professionalization 21 — Calendar-Only Date Inputs
+
+## Objective
+All date entry in the FUSH ERP Mobile UI must be selected from the calendar picker. Manual date typing is not allowed.
+
+## UI policy
+- `FushDateField` is read-only.
+- The displayed/stored value remains the existing `yyyy-MM-dd` string expected by current parsing, reporting, posting, inventory, and service code.
+- Users change a date only through the existing Material 3 date picker action.
+- Optional dates can still be cleared through the picker dialog's Clear action.
+- Required dates cannot be cleared through normal UI interaction.
+- No keyboard is required for date fields.
+
+## Coverage
+The shared field is already used by date inputs introduced/migrated in the UI branch for:
+- Accounting and Treasury: report ranges, as-of dates, manual journal dates, voucher dates.
+- Expenses: report/filter range and expense date.
+- Purchases: invoice date, expiry date, supplier payment date.
+- Inventory: transfer date and expiry/lot assignment dates.
+- Customer/Supplier party vouchers.
+- Geography/currency: FX snapshot date, price-list validity dates, geographic quote date.
+
+Any future date input must use `FushDateField` (or another calendar-only picker) rather than an editable `OutlinedTextField`.
+
+## Safety boundary
+Presentation/input-control only. No database schema, migration, DAO, accounting posting, stock quantity/costing, production, payroll/commission, permissions/authentication, or backup behavior changes.
+
+## Branch test identity
+- versionCode `94`
+- versionName `0.15.4.52.1-ui-calendar-only-dates`
+
+Central integration owns the final integrated version/schema and official APK build/signing.
